                <pb facs="1011" n="879" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg879"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/411: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-15T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                                1926—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>231. Your telegrams 462, October 8, 8 p.m. and 477, October 14, Noon. Department
                    considered that its instructions No. 217, October 5, 7 p.m. sufficiently covered
                    the matter to enable you to join your colleagues in protest outlined in
                    paragraph 3 of your urgent telegram 462, October 8, 8 p.m. No objection to
                    wording of protest as amended is perceived by Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
